   "text": "Scientists have placed reflectors on the Moon. Scientists use the reflectors to measure the\ndistance between the Earth and the Moon.\nreflector\non the Moon\nobservatory\nray of red light\nray of red light\nA scientist in an observatory sends a ray of red light from the observatory to the reflector on\nthe Moon, as shown in Fig. 7.1.\nThe ray takes a total time of 2.5 s to travel from the observatory to the reflector and back to\nthe observatory. The speed of light is 3.0 × 108 m / s.\nCalculate the distance between the observatory and the reflector.\ndistance =  ..................................................... m [3]",
